IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cga-types`
IMPORT `cga-scope`
IMPORT `cga-goods`
IMPORT `cga-services`
IMPORT `cga-goal`

-- Independent tests for the Consumer Guarantees Act 1993 (NZ) encoding.
-- Every expected value comes from independent-expectations.md, written from
-- the source text before the encoding was read. Scenario ids (A1, F14, ...)
-- refer to that file. A failing assertion is a finding, not a bug in this file.

§ `Independent tests`

§§ `Shorthands`

GIVETH A Remedy
`R req` MEANS `require the supplier to remedy the failure within a reasonable time`
GIVETH A Remedy
`R elsewhere` MEANS `have the failure remedied elsewhere and recover the reasonable costs from the supplier`
GIVETH A Remedy
`R reject` MEANS `reject the goods and choose a refund or a replacement`
GIVETH A Remedy
`R sdam` MEANS `damages from the supplier for the reduction in value`
GIVETH A Remedy
`R scons` MEANS `damages from the supplier for reasonably foreseeable consequential loss`
GIVETH A Remedy
`R price` MEANS `refuse to pay more than a reasonable price`
GIVETH A Remedy
`R cancel` MEANS `cancel the contract for the service`
GIVETH A Remedy
`R mdam` MEANS `damages from the manufacturer for the reduction in value`
GIVETH A Remedy
`R mcons` MEANS `damages from the manufacturer for reasonably foreseeable consequential loss`

-- Acquirers (s 2 consumer).
GIVETH AN Acquirer
`acq household` MEANS Acquirer OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
GIVETH AN Acquirer
`acq industrial kind` MEANS Acquirer OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
GIVETH AN Acquirer
`acq resupply` MEANS Acquirer OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
GIVETH AN Acquirer
`acq production` MEANS Acquirer OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
GIVETH AN Acquirer
`acq repairer` MEANS Acquirer OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

-- Contracting-out clauses (s 43(2)).
GIVETH A `Contracting out clause`
`clause valid` MEANS `Contracting out clause` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
GIVETH A `Contracting out clause`
`clause oral` MEANS `Contracting out clause` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
GIVETH A `Contracting out clause`
`clause private buyer` MEANS `Contracting out clause` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
GIVETH A `Contracting out clause`
`clause unfair` MEANS `Contracting out clause` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
GIVETH A `Contracting out clause`
`clause not agreed` MEANS `Contracting out clause` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
GIVETH A `Contracting out clause`
`clause only in trade missing` MEANS `Contracting out clause` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE

-- Supplies.
GIVEN tq IS A `Thing supplied`, tr IS A BOOLEAN, ch IS A BOOLEAN, dt IS A DATE
GIVETH A Supply
`mk supply` tq tr ch dt MEANS Supply OF tq, tr, ch, dt, NOTHING

GIVETH A Supply
`sup goods` MEANS `mk supply` `goods` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2025)

GIVEN cl IS A `Contracting out clause`
GIVETH A Supply
`sup goods with clause` cl MEANS Supply OF `goods`, TRUE, FALSE, Date 1 3 2025, JUST cl

-- A goods failure with the commonly varied facts as parameters.
-- gq: guarantee; rm: can be remedied; rf: supplier refused/failed;
-- sb: s 21(a) substantial; rj: rejected within reasonable time; cq: consequential loss.
GIVEN gq IS A `Goods guarantee`, rm IS A BOOLEAN, rf IS A BOOLEAN, sb IS A BOOLEAN, rj IS A BOOLEAN, cq IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Goods failure`
`gf` gq rm rf sb rj cq MEANS `Goods failure` OF gq, rm, rf, sb, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, rj, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, cq, 1000, 1200, 700

-- A manufacturer-side goods failure.
-- gq: guarantee; s17: manufacturer representation; dm: description by manufacturer;
-- oth: s 26 other person/cause; rrp: s 26(a)(iii) price; eg: express guarantee binding and current;
-- nt: s 42 notice; er: express repair/replace entitlement; mr: manufacturer refused; cq: consequential.
GIVEN gq IS A `Goods guarantee`, s17 IS A BOOLEAN, dm IS A BOOLEAN, oth IS A BOOLEAN, rrp IS A BOOLEAN, eg IS A BOOLEAN, nt IS A BOOLEAN, er IS A BOOLEAN, mr IS A BOOLEAN, cq IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Goods failure`
`mgf` gq s17 dm oth rrp eg nt er mr cq MEANS `Goods failure` OF gq, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, s17, dm, oth, rrp, eg, nt, er, mr, cq, 1000, 1200, 700

-- s 21 limbs and s 20 facts individually.
-- a b c d: s 21(a)-(d); rt: within reasonable time; dp: disposed/lost away; dg: damaged unrelated; at: attached.
GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN, d IS A BOOLEAN, rt IS A BOOLEAN, dp IS A BOOLEAN, dg IS A BOOLEAN, atc IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Goods failure`
`sgf` a b c d rt dp dg atc MEANS `Goods failure` OF `s 6 acceptable quality`, FALSE, FALSE, a, b, c, d, rt, dp, dg, atc, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 1000, 1200, 700

-- Damages facts.
GIVEN pr IS A NUMBER, arp IS A NUMBER, vl IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Goods failure`
`dgf` pr arp vl MEANS `Goods failure` OF `s 6 acceptable quality`, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, pr, arp, vl

-- A service failure.
-- sq: guarantee; rm: can be remedied; rf: refused; a: s 36(a); bb: s 36(b); cc: s 36(c); dd: s 36(d);
-- s33: only because of other person/cause; inc: s 35 incidental; ct: contract; cq: consequential.
GIVEN sq IS A `Service guarantee`, rm IS A BOOLEAN, rf IS A BOOLEAN, a IS A BOOLEAN, bb IS A BOOLEAN, cc IS A BOOLEAN, dd IS A BOOLEAN, s33 IS A BOOLEAN, inc IS A BOOLEAN, ct IS A BOOLEAN, cq IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Service failure`
`sf` sq rm rf a bb cc dd s33 inc ct cq MEANS `Service failure` OF sq, rm, rf, a, bb, cc, dd, s33, inc, ct, cq, 2000, 1200

GIVEN ac IS AN Acquirer, sp IS A Supply, fl IS A `Failure complained of`
GIVETH A `Consumer case`
`mk case` ac sp fl MEANS `Consumer case` OF ac, sp, fl

§§ `A. Who is a consumer (s 2)`

-- A1, A2: household-kind goods, no excluded purpose.
#ASSERT `is a consumer` `acq household` EQUALS TRUE
-- A3: not of a kind ordinarily acquired for personal use.
#ASSERT `is a consumer` `acq industrial kind` EQUALS FALSE
-- A4, A8, A12: resupply in trade (or held out as such).
#ASSERT `is a consumer` `acq resupply` EQUALS FALSE
-- A5: consumed in production.
#ASSERT `is a consumer` `acq production` EQUALS FALSE
-- A6, A7: repairing goods/fixtures in trade.
#ASSERT `is a consumer` `acq repairer` EQUALS FALSE

§§ `B. Goods, buildings, gas and electricity (ss 2, 7B)`

-- B1-B6: goods.
#ASSERT `is within the Act as goods, services, or gas and electricity` `goods` EQUALS TRUE
-- B8: shed, easily removable and non-residential.
#ASSERT `is within the Act as goods, services, or gas and electricity` `a building attached to land, easily removable and not designed for residential accommodation` EQUALS TRUE
-- B7, B9, B10, B11: other buildings attached to land.
#ASSERT `is within the Act as goods, services, or gas and electricity` `a building attached to land, of any other kind` EQUALS FALSE
-- B13, B14: electricity and gas through s 7A.
#ASSERT `is within the Act as goods, services, or gas and electricity` `gas or electricity supplied by a gas or electricity retailer` EQUALS TRUE
-- C1-C4: services.
#ASSERT `is within the Act as goods, services, or gas and electricity` `services` EQUALS TRUE
-- B7 end to end: a house gives no redress.
#ASSERT `the Act gives redress for the supply to` `acq household` `, supply` (`mk supply` `a building attached to land, of any other kind` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2025)) EQUALS FALSE
-- B8 end to end.
#ASSERT `the Act gives redress for the supply to` `acq household` `, supply` (`mk supply` `a building attached to land, easily removable and not designed for residential accommodation` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2025)) EQUALS TRUE

§§ `D. In trade, charities, commencement (ss 41, 56)`

-- D2, D8.
#ASSERT `the Act gives redress for the supply to` `acq household` `, supply` `sup goods` EQUALS TRUE
-- D1: private sale.
#ASSERT `the Act gives redress for the supply to` `acq household` `, supply` (`mk supply` `goods` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2025)) EQUALS FALSE
-- D6: contract made 31 March 1994.
#ASSERT `the Act gives redress for the supply to` `acq household` `, supply` (`mk supply` `goods` TRUE FALSE (Date 31 3 1994)) EQUALS FALSE
-- D7: contract made 1 April 1994.
#ASSERT `the Act gives redress for the supply to` `acq household` `, supply` (`mk supply` `goods` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 4 1994)) EQUALS TRUE
-- D7 variant: 2 April 1994.
#ASSERT `the Act gives redress for the supply to` `acq household` `, supply` (`mk supply` `goods` TRUE FALSE (Date 2 4 1994)) EQUALS TRUE
-- D3: charity, principal purpose to benefit the recipient: no redress against the charity.
#ASSERT `the Act gives redress for the supply to` `acq household` `, supply` (`mk supply` `goods` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2025)) EQUALS FALSE
-- Not a consumer.
#ASSERT `the Act gives redress for the supply to` `acq resupply` `, supply` `sup goods` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the Act gives redress for the supply to` `acq industrial kind` `, supply` `sup goods` EQUALS FALSE

§§ `E. Contracting out (ss 43, 43A)`

-- E1, E11.
#ASSERT `the clause validly contracts out under s 43(2)` `clause valid` EQUALS TRUE
-- E2.
#ASSERT `the clause validly contracts out under s 43(2)` `clause oral` EQUALS FALSE
-- E3.
#ASSERT `the clause validly contracts out under s 43(2)` `clause private buyer` EQUALS FALSE
-- E4.
#ASSERT `the clause validly contracts out under s 43(2)` `clause unfair` EQUALS FALSE
-- E5.
#ASSERT `the clause validly contracts out under s 43(2)` `clause not agreed` EQUALS FALSE
-- s 43(2)(b) alone missing.
#ASSERT `the clause validly contracts out under s 43(2)` `clause only in trade missing` EQUALS FALSE
-- E1 end to end: Act excluded.
#ASSERT `the Act gives redress for the supply to` `acq household` `, supply` (`sup goods with clause` `clause valid`) EQUALS FALSE
-- E2, E6 end to end: invalid clause, Act applies.
#ASSERT `the Act gives redress for the supply to` `acq household` `, supply` (`sup goods with clause` `clause oral`) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the Act gives redress for the supply to` `acq household` `, supply` (`sup goods with clause` `clause private buyer`) EQUALS TRUE

§§ `F. Who answers for which goods guarantee (ss 5-17)`

-- Supplier (s 16): ss 5 to 10; not s 11 (own redress), 12, 13.
#ASSERT `the supplier is answerable under Part 2 for` (`gf` `s 5 title` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the supplier is answerable under Part 2 for` (`gf` `s 5A delivery` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the supplier is answerable under Part 2 for` (`gf` `s 6 acceptable quality` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the supplier is answerable under Part 2 for` (`gf` `s 7A acceptable quality of gas or electricity` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the supplier is answerable under Part 2 for` (`gf` `s 8 fitness for a particular purpose` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the supplier is answerable under Part 2 for` (`gf` `s 9 correspondence with description` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the supplier is answerable under Part 2 for` (`gf` `s 10 correspondence with sample` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the supplier is answerable under Part 2 for` (`gf` `s 12 repairs and spare parts` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the supplier is answerable under Part 2 for` (`gf` `s 13 a manufacturer's express guarantee` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
-- F20: s 17 manufacturer's representation (not on packaging).
#ASSERT `the supplier is answerable under Part 2 for` (`mgf` `s 6 acceptable quality` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
-- F21/F22: no s 17 representation.
#ASSERT `the supplier is answerable under Part 2 for` (`mgf` `s 6 acceptable quality` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
-- F37: s 11 price.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`gf` `s 11 price` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `R price`
-- F38, F44: supplier has no Part 2 redress for ss 12, 13.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`gf` `s 12 repairs and spare parts` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`gf` `s 13 a manufacturer's express guarantee` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS EMPTY
-- F20 remedies.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`mgf` `s 6 acceptable quality` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS EMPTY

-- Manufacturer (s 25, s 26, s 42).
-- J5, F14.
#ASSERT `the manufacturer is answerable under Part 3 for` (`mgf` `s 6 acceptable quality` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
-- F20: s 17 does not protect the manufacturer.
#ASSERT `the manufacturer is answerable under Part 3 for` (`mgf` `s 6 acceptable quality` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
-- J1, J2: another person / cause after leaving manufacturer.
#ASSERT `the manufacturer is answerable under Part 3 for` (`mgf` `s 6 acceptable quality` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
-- J3: price above RRP.
#ASSERT `the manufacturer is answerable under Part 3 for` (`mgf` `s 6 acceptable quality` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
-- F28: manufacturer's description.
#ASSERT `the manufacturer is answerable under Part 3 for` (`mgf` `s 9 correspondence with description` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
-- F29: supplier's own description.
#ASSERT `the manufacturer is answerable under Part 3 for` (`mgf` `s 9 correspondence with description` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
-- J4: retailer relabelling.
#ASSERT `the manufacturer is answerable under Part 3 for` (`mgf` `s 9 correspondence with description` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
-- F38: s 12, no notice.
#ASSERT `the manufacturer is answerable under Part 3 for` (`mgf` `s 12 repairs and spare parts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
-- F39, F41: s 42 notice.
#ASSERT `the manufacturer is answerable under Part 3 for` (`mgf` `s 12 repairs and spare parts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
-- F44: current binding express guarantee.
#ASSERT `the manufacturer is answerable under Part 3 for` (`mgf` `s 13 a manufacturer's express guarantee` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
-- F45: outside its currency.
#ASSERT `the manufacturer is answerable under Part 3 for` (`mgf` `s 13 a manufacturer's express guarantee` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
-- F27, J17: no manufacturer redress for ss 5, 8, 10; nor 5A, 7A, 11.
#ASSERT `the manufacturer is answerable under Part 3 for` (`mgf` `s 5 title` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the manufacturer is answerable under Part 3 for` (`mgf` `s 8 fitness for a particular purpose` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the manufacturer is answerable under Part 3 for` (`mgf` `s 10 correspondence with sample` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the manufacturer is answerable under Part 3 for` (`mgf` `s 5A delivery` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the manufacturer is answerable under Part 3 for` (`mgf` `s 7A acceptable quality of gas or electricity` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the manufacturer is answerable under Part 3 for` (`mgf` `s 11 price` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE

§§ `G. Supplier remedies (s 18, with ss 5A, 20, 21)`

-- G1: remediable, not substantial, not yet required.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`gf` `s 6 acceptable quality` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `R req`, `R scons`
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`gf` `s 6 acceptable quality` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS LIST `R req`
-- G2, G3: supplier refused or failed.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`gf` `s 6 acceptable quality` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `R req`, `R elsewhere`, `R reject`, `R scons`
-- G2 with the right to reject lost (s 20(1)(a)).
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`gf` `s 6 acceptable quality` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `R req`, `R elsewhere`, `R scons`
-- G4: cannot be remedied.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`gf` `s 6 acceptable quality` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `R reject`, `R sdam`, `R scons`
-- G6: cannot be remedied, right to reject lost.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`gf` `s 6 acceptable quality` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `R sdam`, `R scons`
-- G5: substantial but remediable, not yet required.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`gf` `s 6 acceptable quality` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `R req`, `R reject`, `R sdam`, `R scons`
-- G5': substantial, remediable, supplier refused: each remedy once.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`gf` `s 6 acceptable quality` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `R req`, `R elsewhere`, `R reject`, `R sdam`, `R scons`
-- Title failure (F1), cannot be remedied.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`gf` `s 5 title` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `R reject`, `R sdam`, `R scons`
-- F23: s 8, remediable, refused.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`gf` `s 8 fitness for a particular purpose` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS LIST `R req`, `R elsewhere`, `R reject`
-- F11: delivery, not substantial: only consequential damages.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`gf` `s 5A delivery` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `R scons`
-- F11 variant: remediable and supplier refused; still no s 18(2) remedies.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`gf` `s 5A delivery` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `R scons`
-- F11 variant: cannot be remedied but not substantial: no rejection, no reduction-in-value damages.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`gf` `s 5A delivery` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `R scons`
-- F12: delivery, substantial.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`gf` `s 5A delivery` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `R reject`, `R scons`
-- F12, no foreseeable loss.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`gf` `s 5A delivery` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS LIST `R reject`
-- F12 with right to reject lost.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`gf` `s 5A delivery` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `R scons`
-- B15: s 7A electricity, remediable, not yet required.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`gf` `s 7A acceptable quality of gas or electricity` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `R req`, `R scons`

-- s 18(3)(b) damages.
#ASSERT `the supplier's damages for the reduction in value of` (`dgf` 1000 1200 600) EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `the supplier's damages for the reduction in value of` (`dgf` 1000 800 600) EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `the supplier's damages for the reduction in value of` (`dgf` 1000 1200 1100) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the supplier's damages for the reduction in value of` (`dgf` 1000 1200 1000) EQUALS 0

§§ `H. Loss of the right to reject (s 20)`

-- H1.
#ASSERT `the right to reject still applies to` (`sgf` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
-- H2.
#ASSERT `the right to reject still applies to` (`sgf` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
-- H3, H4.
#ASSERT `the right to reject still applies to` (`sgf` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
-- H7.
#ASSERT `the right to reject still applies to` (`sgf` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
-- H8.
#ASSERT `the right to reject still applies to` (`sgf` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
-- H5, H6, H9, H10 (fact is false: at supplier's agent; damage related to defect; detachable; carrier).
#ASSERT `the right to reject still applies to` (`sgf` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE

§§ `I. Substantial character (ss 21, 36)`

-- I1.
#ASSERT `the goods failure is of a substantial character` (`sgf` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
-- I2.
#ASSERT `the goods failure is of a substantial character` (`sgf` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
-- I4, I6.
#ASSERT `the goods failure is of a substantial character` (`sgf` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
-- I7.
#ASSERT `the goods failure is of a substantial character` (`sgf` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
-- I3, I5, I8.
#ASSERT `the goods failure is of a substantial character` (`sgf` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE

-- I10.
#ASSERT `the service failure is of a substantial character` (`sf` `s 28 reasonable care and skill` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
-- s 36(b).
#ASSERT `the service failure is of a substantial character` (`sf` `s 28 reasonable care and skill` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
-- I12: s 29 purpose made known, unfit, not easily remedied.
#ASSERT `the service failure is of a substantial character` (`sf` `s 29 fitness for a particular purpose` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
-- I12': failure complained of is s 28, but a s 29 purpose was made known and the product is unfit for it ("where section 29 applies").
#ASSERT `the service failure is of a substantial character` (`sf` `s 28 reasonable care and skill` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
-- I9.
#ASSERT `the service failure is of a substantial character` (`sf` `s 30 time of completion` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
-- I11: none.
#ASSERT `the service failure is of a substantial character` (`sf` `s 28 reasonable care and skill` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE

§§ `J. Manufacturer remedies and damages (s 27)`

-- J5, J14: no express repair entitlement.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the manufacturer for` (`mgf` `s 6 acceptable quality` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `R mdam`, `R mcons`
-- J11: express repair entitlement, not yet required: consequential only.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the manufacturer for` (`mgf` `s 13 a manufacturer's express guarantee` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `R mcons`
-- J12, J13: required and refused / not succeeded.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the manufacturer for` (`mgf` `s 13 a manufacturer's express guarantee` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `R mdam`, `R mcons`
-- s 27(2) also applies to a s 6 claim where an express guarantee gives repair/replacement.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the manufacturer for` (`mgf` `s 6 acceptable quality` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS EMPTY
-- J1: not answerable.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the manufacturer for` (`mgf` `s 6 acceptable quality` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS EMPTY
-- J6: price 1000, ARP 1200, value 700.
#ASSERT `the manufacturer's damages for the reduction in value of` (`dgf` 1000 1200 700) EQUALS 300
-- J7: price 1500, ARP 1200, value 700.
#ASSERT `the manufacturer's damages for the reduction in value of` (`dgf` 1500 1200 700) EQUALS 500
-- J8.
#ASSERT `the manufacturer's damages for the reduction in value of` (`dgf` 1000 1000 1000) EQUALS 0
-- J9.
#ASSERT `the manufacturer's damages for the reduction in value of` (`dgf` 1000 1200 1100) EQUALS 0
-- J10: gift, price 0.
#ASSERT `the manufacturer's damages for the reduction in value of` (`dgf` 0 500 100) EQUALS 0

§§ `K. Services (ss 28-38)`

-- K1, K10: s 28, even with a third party's contribution.
#ASSERT `the supplier is answerable for the service failure` (`sf` `s 28 reasonable care and skill` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
-- K8: s 29 only because of a third party.
#ASSERT `the supplier is answerable for the service failure` (`sf` `s 29 fitness for a particular purpose` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
-- K9: s 30 only because of a storm.
#ASSERT `the supplier is answerable for the service failure` (`sf` `s 30 time of completion` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
-- K11: not only because of a third party.
#ASSERT `the supplier is answerable for the service failure` (`sf` `s 29 fitness for a particular purpose` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
-- K7: s 31 price.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for the service failure` (`sf` `s 31 price` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `R price`
-- K8 remedies.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for the service failure` (`sf` `s 30 time of completion` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS EMPTY
-- K12.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for the service failure` (`sf` `s 28 reasonable care and skill` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `R req`, `R scons`
-- K13.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for the service failure` (`sf` `s 28 reasonable care and skill` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `R req`, `R elsewhere`, `R cancel`, `R scons`
-- K13': refused, but no contract between supplier and consumer: nothing to cancel.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for the service failure` (`sf` `s 28 reasonable care and skill` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `R req`, `R elsewhere`, `R scons`
-- K14.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for the service failure` (`sf` `s 28 reasonable care and skill` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `R cancel`, `R sdam`, `R scons`
-- K15.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for the service failure` (`sf` `s 28 reasonable care and skill` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `R sdam`, `R scons`
-- K16: incidental to goods the consumer may reject.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for the service failure` (`sf` `s 28 reasonable care and skill` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `R sdam`, `R scons`
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for the service failure` (`sf` `s 28 reasonable care and skill` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS LIST `R req`, `R elsewhere`
-- Substantial, remediable, refused, contract: each remedy once.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for the service failure` (`sf` `s 28 reasonable care and skill` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `R req`, `R elsewhere`, `R cancel`, `R sdam`, `R scons`
-- Substantial, remediable, not yet required.
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for the service failure` (`sf` `s 28 reasonable care and skill` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS LIST `R req`, `R cancel`, `R sdam`
-- s 32(b)(ii) damages: charge 2000, value 1200.
#ASSERT `the damages for the reduction in value of the product of` (`sf` `s 28 reasonable care and skill` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS 800
-- K19, K20 and full retention.
#ASSERT `the refund on cancelling, paid` 2000 `, ordered retained` 0 EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `the refund on cancelling, paid` 2000 `, ordered retained` 500 EQUALS 1500
#ASSERT `the refund on cancelling, paid` 2000 `, ordered retained` 2000 EQUALS 0
-- K21: s 37(1).
#ASSERT `the day the cancellation takes effect, made known` (JUST (Date 5 5 2025)) `, intention indicated` (Date 3 5 2025) `, practicable to tell the supplier:` TRUE EQUALS Date 5 5 2025
#ASSERT `the day the cancellation takes effect, made known` NOTHING `, intention indicated` (Date 3 5 2025) `, practicable to tell the supplier:` FALSE EQUALS Date 3 5 2025
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the day the cancellation takes effect, made known` NOTHING `, intention indicated` (Date 3 5 2025) `, practicable to tell the supplier:` TRUE)

§§ `L. Assignees and creditors (s 46)`

-- L1.
#ASSERT `the most an assignee or creditor is liable for, claim` 5000 `, owing at the date` 3000 EQUALS 3000
-- L2.
#ASSERT `the most an assignee or creditor is liable for, claim` 2000 `, owing at the date` 3000 EQUALS 2000
-- L3.
#ASSERT `the most an assignee or creditor is liable for, claim` 10000 `, owing at the date` 8000 EQUALS 8000
-- L4.
#ASSERT `the most an assignee or creditor is liable for, claim` 3000 `, owing at the date` 3000 EQUALS 3000

§§ `M. Courts (s 47)`

-- M1.
#ASSERT `the forums for a claim of` 60000 EQUALS LIST `the High Court`, `the District Court`, `the Disputes Tribunal`
-- M2.
#ASSERT `the forums for a claim of` 60001 EQUALS LIST `the High Court`, `the District Court`
-- M2 (cents).
#ASSERT `the forums for a claim of` 60000.01 EQUALS LIST `the High Court`, `the District Court`
-- M3.
#ASSERT `the forums for a claim of` 350000 EQUALS LIST `the High Court`, `the District Court`
-- M4.
#ASSERT `the forums for a claim of` 350001 EQUALS LIST `the High Court`
-- M5.
#ASSERT `the forums for a claim of` 500 EQUALS LIST `the High Court`, `the District Court`, `the Disputes Tribunal`

§§ `N. The top-level position`

GIVETH A `Consumer case`
`case fridge` MEANS `mk case` `acq household` `sup goods` (`a failure of goods` (`gf` `s 6 acceptable quality` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE))

-- F14, J6: fridge, s 6 manufacturing defect that cannot be remedied; price 1000, ARP 1200, value 700.
#ASSERT `the consumer guarantees position for` `case fridge` EQUALS `Consumer guarantees position` OF TRUE, TRUE, (LIST `R reject`, `R sdam`, `R scons`), (LIST `R mdam`, `R mcons`), 300, 300

-- D1: private sale.
#ASSERT `the consumer guarantees position for` (`mk case` `acq household` (`mk supply` `goods` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2025)) (`a failure of goods` (`gf` `s 6 acceptable quality` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE))) EQUALS `Consumer guarantees position` OF FALSE, TRUE, EMPTY, EMPTY, 0, 0

-- A4: not a consumer.
#ASSERT `the consumer guarantees position for` (`mk case` `acq resupply` `sup goods` (`a failure of goods` (`gf` `s 6 acceptable quality` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE))) EQUALS `Consumer guarantees position` OF FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, EMPTY, 0, 0

-- E1: validly contracted out (benefit also to the manufacturer, s 43).
#ASSERT (`the consumer guarantees position for` (`mk case` `acq household` (`sup goods with clause` `clause valid`) (`a failure of goods` (`gf` `s 6 acceptable quality` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE))))'s `remedies against the manufacturer` EQUALS EMPTY

-- D3 + s 41(2): charity supplying for the recipient's benefit. No redress against the charity,
-- but s 41(2) does not touch the manufacturer's Part 3 liability.
#ASSERT (`the consumer guarantees position for` (`mk case` `acq household` (`mk supply` `goods` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2025)) (`a failure of goods` (`gf` `s 6 acceptable quality` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE))))'s `remedies against the supplier` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT (`the consumer guarantees position for` (`mk case` `acq household` (`mk supply` `goods` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2025)) (`a failure of goods` (`gf` `s 6 acceptable quality` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE))))'s `remedies against the manufacturer` EQUALS LIST `R mdam`, `R mcons`

-- A13: a repairer in trade acquiring a household-kind *service*; s 2 consumer (b)(iii) applies only "in the case of goods".
#ASSERT (`the consumer guarantees position for` (`mk case` `acq repairer` (`mk supply` `services` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2025)) (`a failure of a service` (`sf` `s 28 reasonable care and skill` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE))))'s `the Act gives redress` EQUALS TRUE

-- B15: electricity, s 7A failure, remediable: Part 2 against the retailer; no manufacturer.
#ASSERT `the consumer guarantees position for` (`mk case` `acq household` (`mk supply` `gas or electricity supplied by a gas or electricity retailer` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2025)) (`a failure of goods` (`gf` `s 7A acceptable quality of gas or electricity` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE))) EQUALS `Consumer guarantees position` OF TRUE, TRUE, (LIST `R req`, `R scons`), EMPTY, 0, 0

-- K services end to end: cannot be remedied, contract; charge 2000, value 1200.
#ASSERT `the consumer guarantees position for` (`mk case` `acq household` (`mk supply` `services` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2025)) (`a failure of a service` (`sf` `s 28 reasonable care and skill` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE))) EQUALS `Consumer guarantees position` OF TRUE, TRUE, (LIST `R cancel`, `R sdam`, `R scons`), EMPTY, 800, 0

-- F20 end to end: s 17 bars the supplier; the manufacturer still answers.
#ASSERT `the consumer guarantees position for` (`mk case` `acq household` `sup goods` (`a failure of goods` (`mgf` `s 6 acceptable quality` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE))) EQUALS `Consumer guarantees position` OF TRUE, TRUE, EMPTY, (LIST `R mdam`, `R mcons`), 0, 300

-- B19: a claim under s 6 for reticulated electricity. s 7B(4): s 7A is the only guarantee, so the Act answers "no redress under s 6"
-- (expected EMPTY; the encoding may refuse instead, which shows as "assertion refused").
#ASSERT (`the consumer guarantees position for` (`mk case` `acq household` (`mk supply` `gas or electricity supplied by a gas or electricity retailer` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2025)) (`a failure of goods` (`gf` `s 6 acceptable quality` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE))))'s `remedies against the supplier` EQUALS EMPTY

-- K24, ss 15, 34: work-and-materials contract recorded as a supply of services; the goods supplied fail s 6 and cannot be remedied.
-- "The guarantees in this Part apply whether or not the goods are supplied in connection with a service."
#ASSERT (`the consumer guarantees position for` (`mk case` `acq household` (`mk supply` `services` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2025)) (`a failure of goods` (`gf` `s 6 acceptable quality` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE))))'s `remedies against the supplier` EQUALS LIST `R reject`, `R sdam`, `R scons`
